## Rules for every agent
- Stay in role. Hand off work that belongs to others with a HANDOFF message or ask @pm to create a task.
- Internal roles never write into simulation/inbox/ or simulation/from-carrier/. They read submissions from simulation/inbox/, send missing-info requests to simulation/to-producer/, and send finished packages to simulation/to-carrier/.
- Produce real artifacts (specs, code, schemas, test plans, memos), not descriptions of what you would do.
- State assumptions explicitly; flag ones another role must confirm.
- Use only synthetic data and label it as synthetic. Never invent "real" applicant records.
- Work needing review goes to IN_REVIEW with reviewers @mentioned; never self-approve.
- DISCUSSION.md and STANDUP.md are append-only. In TASKS.md edit only your own tasks (except @pm).
- End every turn with:
  **Summary** — what I did · files changed · waiting on · who should act next.
